.	http://www.emsl.pnl.gov/ecce:annotation		Quantum ESPRESSO, PBE, plane waves, the conventional cubic cell. This calculation shows that potassium chloride gives a powder pattern with almost no 111 line, like a primitive cubic lattice with half the cell edge: K+ and Cl- have the same number of electrons, so they scatter X-rays alike and look like one kind of atom.
.	http://www.emsl.pnl.gov/ecce:application		QuantumESPRESSO
